speechtext:
With reference to the item:
Kimonas, petticoats and waists in excess of twelve dollars each;
There is also another item on page 7, lime 27, which reads as follows:
Silk clothing, including artificial silk clothing, not elsewhere specified1;
The item now under consideration refers to petticoats and waists in excess of twelve dollars each. A large proportion of these articles are now made of silk, amid you will notice that the other item I refer to deals with silk clothing not elsewhere specified. In view of the fact that so much of this line of merchandise is made of silk, it will follow that all silk waists and petticoats will come under the latter item. I would suggest that the words. " petticoats .and waists .made of silk and other material" be inserted to avoid any difficulty in determining which of these two items will apply.
